        <headline>DUTY TSRV - DUAL BLEED ALERT - W.O CANNOT BE PUSHED</headline>
        <description>W/O TO BE PERFORMED BY DUE DATE OR TO REMAIN AOG UNTIL ACTIONED

BACKGROUND: A DUAL BLEED ALERT HAS BEEN TRIGGERED FOR THIS AIRCRAFT. A REVIEW OF ACMS DATA HAS FOUND LH DUCT PRESSURE LOW DURING TAKEOFF BUT RECOVERING DURING CLIMB AND RH LOW PX ON APPROACH

ACTION:  
1. GAIN ACCESS TO THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS.  

2. USING PNEUMATIC TESTING KIT (P/N 1945-04-08) PERFORM A COMPLETE PNEUMATIC HEALTH CHECK OF THE #2 BLEED COMPONENTS IAW AMM 36-11-00.

* RECORD THE RESULTS ON THE ATTACHED RA851 FORM AND SUBMIT TO BLEEDREVIEW@RYANAIR.COM  
	
** RECORD THE SERIAL NUMBER OF THE TEST KIT USED ON THE RA851 FORM ALSO.

3. INSPECT ALL SYSTEM SENSE LINES AND CONNECTIONS FOR ANY SIGNS OF DAMAGE, BLOCKAGE OR LEAKAGE. MAKE THE NECESSARY RECTIFICATIONS.

4. ENERGIZED APU, SELECT APU BLEED AIR OPEN, MANUALLY WRENCH PRSOV AND LEAK CHECK TO ALL SENSE LINES. SPECIAL ATTENTION TO PRSOV DOWNSTREAM SENSE LINE PN 16135-81 FOR LEAKAGE.

5. LEAK CHECK ALL HSR / HSV / PCCV / BAR SENSE LINES USING SUITABLE LEAK CHECK SPRAY.

6. CLOSELY INSPECT RH PRSOV FOR NOTCHY BEHAVIOUR, INABILITY TO REMAIN OPEN AND ACTUATOR BODY LEAKAGE.

7. CHECK BLEED AIR REGULATOR FOR D/S PORT LEAKAGE OR RUPTURED REVERSE FLOW DIAPHRAGM.

8. REPLACE ANY FAULTY COMPONENT FOUND IAW AMM. 
	IF NFF REPLACE THE #2 PCCV IAW AMM 36-12-02/401 - LATEST REV

9. RETURN THE AIRCRAFT TO SERVICE.   

**AIRCRAFT IS EQUIPPED WITH ACMS - NO BLEED SHEETS WILL BE REQUIRED.  

**PLEASE ENSURE THAT ALL ELECTRICAL (WHERE APPLICABLE) AND PNEUMATIC FITTINGS / COMPONENTS DISTURBED DURING ABOVE WORKS ARE RE-INSTATED TO CORRECT CONFIGURATION AFTER WORKS.</description>
